WEBVTT

1
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:28.630
Shit.

2
00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:35.553
Shit.

3
00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:36.679
(SCATTING)

4
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.724
POPPY: Molly? Molly.

5
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.018
- Molly!
- Hey, I was listening to that.

6
00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.821
Earth calling sisterling.
Have you forgotten

7
00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.521
today's the day
Rosemary moves in?

8
00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:49.275
Like you'd let me forget? Please tell me
you're not going to do anything crazy.

9
00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.651
Look, you know I love you, Mollster,

10
00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:53.488
but there are some things
you're just way too young to understand.

11
00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:55.364
I know what I'm doing, though, okay?

12
00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:57.200
- Trust me.
- Poppy!

13
00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:06.918
All right, guys. Let's give my dad's
girlfriend the perfect Malibu welcome.

14
00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:09.504
Everyone, help yourselves!

15
00:02:09.588 --> 00:02:11.380
(ALL WHOOPING)

16
00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:17.762
You can keep it, or you can throw it away!
Let's go, you guys. You can keep that.

17
00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:20.515
GIRL 1: I want the bouncy ball!
POPPY: You get those. We don't need them.

18
00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.851
- All right, let's get rid of it!
- GIRL 2: That dress is so hot!

19
00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:26.938
Oh, Poppy, you've really done it this time.

20
00:02:28.482 --> 00:02:29.565
Ugh!

21
00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:33.945
Hey, girls! Watch this!

22
00:02:38.951 --> 00:02:40.368
(ALL GASPING)

23
00:02:40.452 --> 00:02:42.245
(GIRLS SCREAMING)

24
00:02:52.256 --> 00:02:54.841
GIRL 1: Where did she go?
GIRL 2: Is she okay?

25
00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:56.342
GIRL 1: Is she still down there?
RODDY: She's still under.

26
00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:59.053
GIRL 2: There might be sharks.
GIRL 3: Someone do something.

27
00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:01.556
Welcome to Malibu, biatch!

28
00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:07.061
GERRY: Excuse me, excuse me.

29
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.401
Get up here, right now. Get up here!

30
00:03:14.862 --> 00:03:16.779
Please, go home. Home, home.

31
00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:18.531
GIRL 1: So uncool.
BOY 1: Easy, pops.

32
00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:21.284
GERRY: Go on. Out, out.
BOY 2: Yo, Dad.

33
00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:24.704
- GIRL 2: Loser.
- Out, out, out. Let's go. Out, out.

34
00:03:24.788 --> 00:03:29.208
That is the final straw, Poppy.
You are going to England.

35
00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:32.378
- Let's go.
- Yawn. The boarding school threat again.

36
00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:36.841
I don't even recognize you anymore.
All this is going to stop right now!

37
00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.467
So what? Big deal!

38
00:03:38.552 --> 00:03:42.346
You can just replace me with a newer,
trashier version, like you did with Mom!

39
00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:46.809
You are going to boarding school
in England, and that's final.

40
00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:49.604
What? You think just because Mom
went to boarding school in England,

41
00:03:49.688 --> 00:03:55.151
it's going to magically straighten me out?
Do you even remember Mom?

42
00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:59.196
(SIGHING)

43
00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:07.246
Hi, Molly.

44
00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:12.376
I think you might've
pushed him too far this time.

45
00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:15.755
I know.

46
00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:20.760
But England's so far away.

47
00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:26.974
Well, at least
they speak American there, right?

48
00:04:27.059 --> 00:04:30.519
But who's going to cut
the crusts off my sandwiches?

49
00:04:31.897 --> 00:04:36.067
You're going to be fine, Moll. I promise.

50
00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.451
In England, it rains 200
days out of the year.

51
00:04:45.535 --> 00:04:49.121
- You will definitely get SAD.
- She is sad.

52
00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.499
(SCOFFS) Seasonal affected disorder.

53
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:55.670
Depression due to lack of sunlight,
resulting in acne and weight gain.

54
00:04:55.754 --> 00:04:58.714
- POPPY: What?
- What? I saw it on Dr. 90210.

55
00:05:00.425 --> 00:05:05.388
(GASPS) Not those shoes.
They don't do rain.

56
00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:09.058
Just take them.

57
00:05:09.184 --> 00:05:12.019
Hey, you promise we'll talk every day?
Swear on your life?

58
00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:17.274
Dude, who loves ya?
Everything's going to suck without you.

59
00:05:17.401 --> 00:05:20.903
POPPY: Ruby, you're my best friend.
I'm going to miss you so much.

60
00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.198
I know, let's check out their website.

61
00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.910
(TYPING)

62
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:32.581
- Oh, my God!
- Oh, my God!

63
00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:36.919
"Abbey Mount School is
an independent boarding school

64
00:05:37.004 --> 00:05:39.964
- "for girls aged 11 to 17."
- Oh, my God.

65
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.758
POPPY: "Founded in 1797",

66
00:05:42.843 --> 00:05:46.929
"the school is one of England's
top institutions for young ladies."

67
00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:51.017
It's all brick! Please tell me
that's not in the countryside.

68
00:05:59.985 --> 00:06:01.027
Ugh!

69
00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.787
Excuse me.

70
00:06:22.883 --> 00:06:24.884
Hello. How are you?

71
00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.719
- All right, Kate?
- Yes, thanks.

72
00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:27.970
MRS. KINGSLEY: Very good.

73
00:06:32.559 --> 00:06:34.894
Mr. Moore? I'm Mrs. Kingsley.

74
00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:39.315
Oh, please, call me Gerry. Thank you.
I am so grateful.

75
00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:45.154
- I'm happy we could help out. - She's
going through rather a difficult stage.

76
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:50.117
Just leave it to me, Mr. Moore.
I have a double first in difficult.

77
00:06:52.079 --> 00:06:54.705
- Hello, how are you?
- Hi.

78
00:06:54.831 --> 00:06:56.332
- Good holiday?
- GIRL 1: Yeah.

79
00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.666
Good.

80
00:07:02.506 --> 00:07:07.051
Hello, Poppy. Welcome to Abbey Mount.
I'm Mrs. Kingsley, your headmistress.

81
00:07:07.124 --> 00:07:08.445
Look, I understand you're just...

82
00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.970
Uh-uh, uh-uh.

83
00:07:10.847 --> 00:07:15.518
Lesson number one, Poppy.
To me negotiation is like a nightclub.

84
00:07:15.602 --> 00:07:19.438
Not something I tend to enter into.
Now come along.

85
00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.566
- Hello.
- Hi.

86
00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:24.693
How are you?

87
00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.992
Wow.

88
00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:33.369
GIRL 1: Who's she?
GIRL 2: Wow.

89
00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.870
Is she new?

90
00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:38.249
- Wow.
- GIRL 3: Look at those shoes.

91
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:39.708
GIRL 4: Look at her.

92
00:07:41.044 --> 00:07:44.338
Poppy, this is Kate.
She'll be your big sister at Abbey Mount.

93
00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:46.382
You'll soon settle in.

94
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.718
- Hi, how do you do?
- I already have a sister.

95
00:07:49.803 --> 00:07:52.721
It's just school lingo. I'll be your
friend, a helping hand, that's all.

96
00:07:52.806 --> 00:07:58.144
Okay, but I choose my friends,
and FYI, you don't make the cut.

97
00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:02.231
I'm sure that comment would sting
a lot more if I knew what FYI meant.

98
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:07.236
But, for the moment, let's just pretend
it's had the desired effect, shall we?

99
00:08:08.697 --> 00:08:12.199
Saddle up, girls.
We've got ourselves a bronco.

100
00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:15.703
Mrs. Kingsley, a gift.

101
00:08:15.787 --> 00:08:18.414
One for you and one for Freddie.

102
00:08:18.874 --> 00:08:19.915
Oh.

103
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:23.043
- Thank you.
- I shot them myself.

104
00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:25.421
Oh, I don't doubt that you did.

105
00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:29.300
Well, perhaps you'd like to keep a hold of
them while I welcome back the first years.

106
00:08:29.384 --> 00:08:31.343
Nice thought, though.

107
00:08:39.561 --> 00:08:42.188
(HARRIET SPEAKING LATIN)

108
00:08:42.564 --> 00:08:44.690
Harriet. Head Girl.

109
00:08:47.152 --> 00:08:51.071
You shake the hand of the Head Girl
out of respect.

110
00:08:51.156 --> 00:08:56.035
When the Head Girl has earned my respect,
then I'll shake her hand, biatch.

111
00:08:56.119 --> 00:08:58.454
- I'm sorry?
- Apology accepted.

112
00:09:03.627 --> 00:09:07.630
Stunningly horridious ego
desperately seeks a good bashing.

113
00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:10.132
Can we oblige? Methinks so.

114
00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:13.198
JANE AND CHARLOTTE: We think so, too.

115
00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:18.641
I'll call you tomorrow morning,
as soon as I'm back in LA.

116
00:09:18.725 --> 00:09:20.976
I hope your flight gets seriously delayed.

117
00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:22.603
(CHUCKLES)

118
00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:25.731
And I hope your bags end up in Kazakhstan.

119
00:09:29.027 --> 00:09:32.947
I'll come back for you
at the end of the semester, all right?

120
00:09:33.031 --> 00:09:36.408
Sweetheart, you know I love you.

121
00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.208
(CAR ENGINE STARTING)

122
00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.877
Bye.

123
00:10:06.773 --> 00:10:08.691
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

124
00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:10.567
(SIGHING)

125
00:10:14.956 --> 00:10:16.156
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING ON STEREO)

126
00:10:16.157 --> 00:10:17.616
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING ON STEREO)

127
00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:21.328
DRIPPY: I have to find this CD to play
for you guys. There it is.

128
00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:23.455
You can borrow them, but only indoors.

129
00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.250
DRIPPY: Yeah, my mum won't let me
wear high heels.

130
00:10:26.334 --> 00:10:29.086
JOSIE: I've got to be reserve
because I'm not there all the time.

131
00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.754
KIKI: I heard this on the radio.

132
00:10:30.839 --> 00:10:32.381
- Thank you.
- DRIPPY: Nice catch.

133
00:10:36.511 --> 00:10:37.970
Excuse me.

134
00:10:40.181 --> 00:10:43.726
Hi. I've been assigned this room.

135
00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:47.479
You need to leave.

136
00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:52.401
Oh, wow, communal.

137
00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:56.864
Well, it's bed number five or the corridor.
Your choice, mate.

138
00:10:59.409 --> 00:11:02.161
Move your stinking socks, Drippy.

139
00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:09.585
(EXCLAIMS IN DISGUST)

140
00:11:10.587 --> 00:11:11.628
Gross.

141
00:11:13.048 --> 00:11:14.757
(GIRLS CHATTERING)

142
00:11:18.678 --> 00:11:21.263
You lock away your chocolate?

143
00:11:21.389 --> 00:11:25.017
Key information, if it's
the Wagon Wheel versus the Rolex,

144
00:11:25.101 --> 00:11:27.853
the Wagon Wheel is going to
trounce it every time.

145
00:11:27.937 --> 00:11:32.107
- What's a Wagon Wheel?
- Jesu Christi, you have not lived!

146
00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:40.491
- Ew! That's carbs and sugar.
- What a revelation. I had no idea.

147
00:11:42.911 --> 00:11:44.870
(CELL PHONE BEEPING)

148
00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:50.334
- What the bleep is that?
- None of your bleeping business.

149
00:11:50.418 --> 00:11:51.668
It's an iPhone.

150
00:11:51.753 --> 00:11:56.215
Good luck getting a signal. We only have
two hot spots that work round here.

151
00:11:56.299 --> 00:11:59.718
Maybe you should try entering
the 21st century, Buck Rogers.

152
00:11:59.803 --> 00:12:03.722
This place is medieval.
It's imperative that I make my phone calls.

153
00:12:03.807 --> 00:12:07.518
It's pointless anyway.
We're only allowed mobiles on weekends.

154
00:12:07.602 --> 00:12:09.728
How am I supposed to call my therapist?

155
00:12:09.813 --> 00:12:10.896
(GIRLS CHUCKLING)

156
00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:16.402
She's joking, right? Oh, sweetheart,
this is not Beverly Hills, 90210.

157
00:12:16.486 --> 00:12:19.738
Just put it away before Matron catches you.

158
00:12:19.823 --> 00:12:22.991
- Where's your trunk?
- Hasn't been delivered yet.

159
00:12:39.175 --> 00:12:40.759
(POPPY EXCLAIMS)

160
00:12:40.844 --> 00:12:42.511
No.

161
00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:48.350
No, no, no. Not the new season Gucci. No.
The Choos. No!

162
00:12:48.435 --> 00:12:52.062
This is all only hand-washable.
This is ridiculous.

163
00:12:52.147 --> 00:12:55.107
- Why...
- What? I might get thirsty.

164
00:12:55.191 --> 00:12:58.944
You know, in the UK we have this
amazing thing. It's called a tap.

165
00:13:02.157 --> 00:13:04.366
Welcome back, girls.

166
00:13:04.492 --> 00:13:08.787
Oh, good, staff. How quickly
can you get all this stuff cleaned?

167
00:13:08.872 --> 00:13:10.539
- Is she...
- American.

168
00:13:10.665 --> 00:13:15.544
Oh, yes, we had one of those in 1997.
Not good.

169
00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:19.882
Accustom her to my rules, and she should
be in the correct uniform for a start.

170
00:13:20.008 --> 00:13:22.301
Mobile phones, please, girls.

171
00:13:24.471 --> 00:13:27.473
Thank you, Kiki. Thank you, Josie.
Thank you, Kate.

172
00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:31.894
Whoa! Hands off, mama. I said, hands off.

173
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.230
(POPPY QUESTIONING IN SPANISH)

174
00:13:36.983 --> 00:13:39.234
I am Scottish, not remedial.

175
00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:43.989
Good, then you understand.
Line dry, press, no starch, and no creases.

176
00:13:44.073 --> 00:13:46.783
How dare you? No mufti for a week.

177
00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:49.786
Fine. Mufti may be your thing, lady,
but it sure ain't mine.

178
00:13:49.913 --> 00:13:53.790
- She means no home clothes for a week.
- Like I give a shit.

179
00:13:53.917 --> 00:13:55.709
- I'll be gone by then.
- Language!

180
00:13:55.793 --> 00:13:57.433
Two Sundays detention.
For the whole dorm.

181
00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:58.837
(GIRLS SIGH)

182
00:13:58.922 --> 00:14:01.173
I'll deal with this. Look, hey. Hey.

183
00:14:01.257 --> 00:14:05.344
Here's a Ben Franklin.
Why don't you go out and buy yourself...

184
00:14:05.428 --> 00:14:10.057
Well, anything. Whatever you get
will be a serious improvement.

185
00:14:10.141 --> 00:14:13.435
Three Sundays. For everyone.

186
00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.521
(GIRLS GROANING)

187
00:14:16.564 --> 00:14:20.734
- Thanks a lot for that, you utter moron.
- What are you, mental?

188
00:14:20.818 --> 00:14:25.155
What? She was a grade one a-hole
with a severe attitudinal problem.

189
00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:29.243
The bell's going to go in a minute.
Just put your uniform on.

190
00:14:29.786 --> 00:14:31.245
(BELL RINGING)

191
00:14:31.329 --> 00:14:32.621
Now!

192
00:14:33.748 --> 00:14:36.583
KATE: You will never get away
with that uniform, for start,

193
00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:40.504
and FYI, no drinking, no smoking,
no alcohol.

194
00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.925
No fireworks, no dangerous weapons,
no illegal drugs.

195
00:14:45.009 --> 00:14:48.679
If you have a problem with someone,
no random bitching. Structure your point.

196
00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:51.473
No Web surfing, no bullying.

197
00:14:51.599 --> 00:14:55.227
So, if you behave like an arsehole, we all
suffer, so do not get us in your shit

198
00:14:55.311 --> 00:14:58.146
- or we will break you.
- Oh, I'm scared.

199
00:14:58.648 --> 00:15:01.441
- GIRLS: Hi, Kate. Hi, how
are you? Hi, Kate! - Hello.

200
00:15:01.526 --> 00:15:04.653
What are you, like,
prom queen or something?

201
00:15:04.779 --> 00:15:06.238
Kate's got a terrible affliction.

202
00:15:06.322 --> 00:15:09.658
You're actually lucky that you don't
have it. It's called popularity.

203
00:15:09.784 --> 00:15:12.202
Hey, get up.
Wait for Mrs. Kingsley and the prefects.

204
00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:13.829
Screw them.

205
00:15:16.207 --> 00:15:18.917
That's physical abuse.
I'm calling my lawyer.

206
00:15:19.002 --> 00:15:20.168
With what?

207
00:15:21.629 --> 00:15:24.590
Well, hello, Freddie.

208
00:15:24.674 --> 00:15:28.635
How kind of you to grace us
with your gorgeous presence.

209
00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.973
And cue Harriet in three, two, one...

210
00:15:33.057 --> 00:15:37.019
- Subject's moved in on target.
- And we have contact.

211
00:15:39.814 --> 00:15:41.648
- Walk, Annabelle.
- Walk, Annabelle.

212
00:15:41.733 --> 00:15:43.400
(BOTH CHUCKLING)

213
00:15:46.529 --> 00:15:49.170
DRIPPY: I love that Freddie's always here
at the beginning of term.

214
00:15:49.198 --> 00:15:51.700
Such a perfect welcome back.

215
00:15:51.826 --> 00:15:54.453
- So, who is Freddie?
- Mrs. Kingsley's son.

216
00:15:54.537 --> 00:15:57.178
Devastating heartthrob.
Won't look at any of us since he got caught

217
00:15:57.206 --> 00:16:01.293
playing doctors and nurses with a girl
in the third grade when he was 11.

218
00:16:01.377 --> 00:16:02.961
Massive hoo-hah.

219
00:16:03.046 --> 00:16:05.797
- They're not together now, though.
- 'Cause of her massive hoo-hah?

220
00:16:08.009 --> 00:16:11.470
No. Fraternizing is forbidden.

221
00:16:11.554 --> 00:16:13.096
WAITRESS: Here you go.

222
00:16:16.726 --> 00:16:19.936
- I can't eat this.
- Anorexia or bulimia?

223
00:16:20.063 --> 00:16:23.273
Because if it's bulimia we'd rather
you didn't eat other people's birthday cake

224
00:16:23.358 --> 00:16:25.817
on their birthdays. It's such a waste.

225
00:16:25.902 --> 00:16:29.738
Actually, I'm a pescetarian
Monday through Wednesday,

226
00:16:29.864 --> 00:16:33.784
fruitarian Thursday through Sunday
and vegetarian always.

227
00:16:36.913 --> 00:16:38.622
For what we are about to receive...

228
00:16:38.706 --> 00:16:40.832
(CHANTING)

229
00:16:45.755 --> 00:16:47.214
ALL: Amen.

230
00:16:47.382 --> 00:16:48.757
(SPEAKING HINDI)

231
00:17:04.482 --> 00:17:08.026
- KATE: (WHISPERS) Get out of the way!
- Hey, watch the shmere, girlfriend.

232
00:17:08.111 --> 00:17:10.278
Two hundred goats died for this.

233
00:17:10.405 --> 00:17:14.908
We meet again. How sublime.
Learn the rules.

234
00:17:14.992 --> 00:17:18.036
When it comes to right of way,
there is a hierarchy.

235
00:17:18.121 --> 00:17:23.667
Teachers, prefects, scholars,
dogs, vermin, Americans.

236
00:17:24.794 --> 00:17:28.588
Kate? See to it she falls in line.

237
00:17:30.341 --> 00:17:32.592
What is this place? Hogwarts?

238
00:17:34.971 --> 00:17:37.139
- Bedtime, girls.
- KATE: Night.

239
00:17:38.766 --> 00:17:43.478
The correct school uniform. Wear it. Bed.

240
00:17:44.439 --> 00:17:46.690
Poppy Moore, bed! Now!

241
00:17:54.699 --> 00:17:56.742
(MR. NELLIST GREETING IN FRENCH)

242
00:17:56.826 --> 00:17:58.994
(GIRLS GREETING IN FRENCH)

243
00:18:01.122 --> 00:18:02.914
(PANTING) Right.

244
00:18:02.999 --> 00:18:07.419
Translation today, everyone.
So, PDF, pretty damn straightforward.

245
00:18:07.503 --> 00:18:13.341
Ergo, which means? Anyone? Ergo?

246
00:18:13.676 --> 00:18:16.011
- Oh, Mr. Nellist.
- Yes, Drippy.

247
00:18:16.345 --> 00:18:21.099
- "Er, leave"?
- Luddite. No, it means therefore, Drippy.

248
00:18:21.184 --> 00:18:25.103
Therefore, you'll probably finish early,
which means that you'll have lots of time

249
00:18:25.188 --> 00:18:29.065
to ask me questions about my trip
to Champagne with my girlfriend.

250
00:18:29.192 --> 00:18:34.571
Now, sadly, my ex-girlfriend.
Though she was my girlfriend at the time.

251
00:18:34.655 --> 00:18:36.364
(GIRLS GIGGLING)

252
00:18:39.702 --> 00:18:41.703
Put the headphones on, please.

253
00:18:47.043 --> 00:18:50.962
Hi, guys. You don't happen
to have any eyebrow tint, do you?

254
00:18:51.047 --> 00:18:52.255
GIRLS: No.

255
00:18:52.381 --> 00:18:54.966
Do you guys have any eyebrow tints?

256
00:18:55.051 --> 00:18:57.886
(POP MUSIC PLAYING ON HEADPHONES)

257
00:18:58.888 --> 00:19:03.183
(WHISPERING) Apparently,
California girls wax their bums.

258
00:19:03.267 --> 00:19:05.769
KATE: What? Why?

259
00:19:05.895 --> 00:19:08.647
DRIPPY: To look Brazilian.
Makes it more attractive.

260
00:19:08.731 --> 00:19:10.357
If you say so.

261
00:19:13.027 --> 00:19:17.531
- Do you think she's done it?
- Hundred percent.

262
00:19:17.615 --> 00:19:21.660
She's definitely done the missionary
and almost certainly the Lebanese fulcrum.

263
00:19:21.744 --> 00:19:24.579
- I can tell.
- How?

264
00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:27.249
From the angle of her hips.

265
00:19:32.421 --> 00:19:34.589
Can I help you?

266
00:19:34.715 --> 00:19:38.260
- Is there a problem?
- How many boys have you shagged?

267
00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:45.183
Well, there was Brandon, eight-pack.
Chase, jock.

268
00:19:45.268 --> 00:19:49.938
Tyler. Bajillionaire. Derek.
He was Kelly Slater's cousin.

269
00:19:50.022 --> 00:19:53.441
And, oh, Jack. He was all-around sick.

270
00:19:53.901 --> 00:19:58.280
- Christ.
- I mean sick body, sick mind.

271
00:19:58.364 --> 00:20:02.284
- Shit! Kate! - Sorry, Drip.
- It looked lighter on the box.

272
00:20:04.495 --> 00:20:06.246
(DRIPPY WHINING)

273
00:20:08.416 --> 00:20:12.544
That is butters.
Better not stop me pulling at the social.

274
00:20:12.628 --> 00:20:15.755
Honey, eyebrows are the least
of your worries.

275
00:20:16.424 --> 00:20:19.009
MATRON: Lights out, girls.
Everyone into bed.

276
00:20:19.093 --> 00:20:20.719
KIKI: Night, Matron.
KATE: Night.

277
00:20:20.803 --> 00:20:22.387
(DRIPPY GROANING)

278
00:20:22.471 --> 00:20:26.808
- KATE: Hey, switch that off!
- No wireless. Should have known.

279
00:20:26.893 --> 00:20:29.394
KIKI: Internet is only allowed
in the computer room.

280
00:20:29.478 --> 00:20:31.771
Whoa! We are not allowed
out of bed after lights out.

281
00:20:31.856 --> 00:20:33.899
- Oh, look. They're not out.
- KATE: Hey!

282
00:20:33.983 --> 00:20:36.985
- What are you doing? Get back into bed!
- KIKI: Come back.

283
00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.654
POPPY: Dear Ruby, oh, my God.

284
00:20:39.739 --> 00:20:42.365
Two weeks in this place
and I'm going out of my mind.

285
00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.951
These girls are all ugly losers
who think a mani-pedi

286
00:20:45.036 --> 00:20:47.495
is some kind of Latin greeting.

287
00:20:59.675 --> 00:21:01.468
(DRIPPY GROANING)

288
00:21:32.667 --> 00:21:34.084
Mmm!

289
00:21:34.168 --> 00:21:35.669
(SOFTLY) Ew.

290
00:21:37.588 --> 00:21:39.714
(BELL RINGING)

291
00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.300
- MATRON: Come on! Fire practice!
- Shit!

292
00:21:42.385 --> 00:21:44.345
MATRON: Remove yourselves
to the quad immediately.

293
00:21:44.428 --> 00:21:47.931
Come on.
You know the drill, for goodness sakes.

294
00:21:48.057 --> 00:21:51.393
Come on, stop being so slovenly.
Hurry up. Kiki.

295
00:21:52.395 --> 00:21:54.229
(FIRE ALARM BLARING)

296
00:22:00.277 --> 00:22:02.153
(EXCLAIMS IN DISGUST)

297
00:22:03.572 --> 00:22:05.865
MATRON: Come on, girls! Hurry up!

298
00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:10.412
What if there was a real fire?
We'll all be burned to a crisp.

299
00:22:16.252 --> 00:22:17.335
(WATER SPLASHING)

300
00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:19.254
FREDDIE: Hey, who's there?

301
00:22:21.298 --> 00:22:22.424
Poppy.

302
00:22:23.217 --> 00:22:27.429
- FREDDIE: Last name?
- Moore. Poppy Moore, sir.

303
00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:32.684
Well, Moore, Poppy Moore,
this is a fire practice.

304
00:22:32.768 --> 00:22:36.229
- Sorry, I'm new here.
- FREDDIE: Yes, that's obvious.

305
00:22:36.313 --> 00:22:38.189
But weren't you listening in physics class?

306
00:22:38.274 --> 00:22:40.692
Fire tends to be hot,
and the point is to avoid it.

307
00:22:40.776 --> 00:22:43.653
Okay. Where do I go?

308
00:22:43.738 --> 00:22:46.448
FREDDIE: Out the door, turn left,
and down the stairs.

309
00:22:46.574 --> 00:22:50.118
POPPY: Run towards the bright orange
flickery thing. Right?

310
00:22:50.286 --> 00:22:55.415
- FREDDIE: Oh, and try not to get caught.
- Excellent point, sir.

311
00:23:00.963 --> 00:23:02.839
(RAP SONG PLAYING)

312
00:23:04.258 --> 00:23:05.967
SARA: Lovely, Harriet.

313
00:23:16.645 --> 00:23:17.687
Ew!

314
00:23:24.779 --> 00:23:28.490
Crack on, team. Lovely stick work, Harriet.

315
00:23:31.827 --> 00:23:32.911
Hi.

316
00:23:32.995 --> 00:23:35.163
- Hello, Mr. Nellist.
- MR. NELLIST: Hello, hello.

317
00:23:38.542 --> 00:23:40.668
Well, super, super effort.

318
00:23:40.795 --> 00:23:45.048
We may not win the championships,
but we'll win a lot of friends, yeah?

319
00:23:45.174 --> 00:23:47.133
So bloody English.

320
00:23:48.844 --> 00:23:50.929
Really. And you could do better?

321
00:23:51.013 --> 00:23:55.308
Laugh it up, but I could whip
all of your asses blindfolded.

322
00:23:55.392 --> 00:23:58.353
This I'd love to see.

323
00:23:58.479 --> 00:24:02.690
Oh, it's on like Donkey Kong.
Do your worst, horse face.

324
00:24:25.464 --> 00:24:26.798
(WHISTLES)

325
00:24:26.882 --> 00:24:31.386
(BOTH SHOUTING)

326
00:24:38.352 --> 00:24:40.478
Foul! Body check. Body check!

327
00:24:40.563 --> 00:24:41.771
(HARRIET AND POPPY SCREAMING)

328
00:24:41.856 --> 00:24:43.314
Please!

329
00:24:43.399 --> 00:24:44.482
(CAR HONKING)

330
00:24:44.567 --> 00:24:48.153
- HARRIET: Perfectly legal. - Shouldn't
you guys be in bikinis for that?

331
00:24:48.237 --> 00:24:49.863
Hi, Fredster. Dig the car.

332
00:24:49.947 --> 00:24:51.156
(CAR REVVING)

333
00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:54.284
- Hello, Moore. Poppy Moore.
- Hi.

334
00:24:55.077 --> 00:24:56.161
Hey!

335
00:24:58.914 --> 00:25:00.081
Bye.

336
00:25:01.625 --> 00:25:03.835
Ooh, do you love Fredster?

337
00:25:03.919 --> 00:25:07.505
- Do you want to kiss Fredster on the lips?
- Don't be so immature.

338
00:25:07.590 --> 00:25:11.259
Don't try and hide it, honey.
We've got ourselves a SULA.

339
00:25:11.385 --> 00:25:14.095
Sweaty Upper Lip Alert.

340
00:25:14.221 --> 00:25:16.181
(GIRLS GIGGLING)

341
00:25:16.682 --> 00:25:18.725
(HARRIET WHIMPERS)

342
00:25:19.810 --> 00:25:23.313
How on Earth did Freddie know her name?
You may depart.

343
00:25:23.439 --> 00:25:27.108
- But, I still have to turn down your bed.
- Get out!

344
00:25:29.445 --> 00:25:33.907
I don't understand.
Freddie's got a crush on me.

345
00:25:33.991 --> 00:25:35.658
Why was he looking at her?

346
00:25:35.784 --> 00:25:39.954
He was looking at her
so he didn't come across as looking at you.

347
00:25:40.039 --> 00:25:42.916
He needs to be careful.
He can't get caught.

348
00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:47.337
Yeah, and if he looked at you too much,
he wouldn't be able to control himself.

349
00:25:47.463 --> 00:25:53.384
Like, when I have to look sad, I think
about horses being slaughtered.

350
00:25:53.469 --> 00:25:57.388
So to Freddie, Poppy's the equivalent
of a slaughtered horse.

351
00:25:57.473 --> 00:25:59.474
You're probably right.

352
00:25:59.558 --> 00:26:05.230
But we're going to have to do something
about little Miss USA.

353
00:26:05.314 --> 00:26:09.317
She needs a lesson
in exactly who's boss, methinks.

354
00:26:09.401 --> 00:26:11.152
BOTH: We think so, too.

355
00:26:12.738 --> 00:26:16.741
- I didn't start it. It wasn't my fault.
- Go out and close the door.

356
00:26:16.825 --> 00:26:18.284
But you asked to see me.

357
00:26:18.369 --> 00:26:21.788
Yes, well, you have to knock
before you enter.

358
00:26:21.872 --> 00:26:25.250
POPPY: I can't believe it.
This is all horse face's fault!

359
00:26:25.334 --> 00:26:26.459
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

360
00:26:26.543 --> 00:26:28.836
Who is it?

361
00:26:28.921 --> 00:26:30.505
Jesus Christ!

362
00:26:30.589 --> 00:26:33.424
Oh, dear. We were led to believe
you had a beard and sandals.

363
00:26:33.509 --> 00:26:36.761
Now, we'll have to change that
stained-glass window in the school chapel.

364
00:26:36.845 --> 00:26:39.335
Look, I didn't start it,
it wasn't my fault,

365
00:26:39.348 --> 00:26:41.849
and if this were
America, I would sue.

366
00:26:41.934 --> 00:26:45.728
That girl is a grade one a-hole
with a severe attitudinal problem.

367
00:26:45.854 --> 00:26:48.273
I know perfectly well
what happened, Poppy.

368
00:26:48.357 --> 00:26:49.941
Then why isn't Harriet here too?

369
00:26:50.025 --> 00:26:53.611
Because, unsurprisingly,
it's you I want to talk to.

370
00:26:54.405 --> 00:26:58.950
Look, I know it's very difficult
being the only new girl in your year.

371
00:26:59.034 --> 00:27:01.369
You mean, the only normal girl.

372
00:27:03.038 --> 00:27:08.793
- What do you like to read, Poppy?
- OK Magazine, People, Us Weekly.

373
00:27:08.877 --> 00:27:11.963
Well, might you be able to tackle
such a thing as a book?

374
00:27:12.047 --> 00:27:14.882
- I prefer movies.
- Well, my personal library

375
00:27:14.967 --> 00:27:18.720
seems to be missing
the book version of Freaky Friday.

376
00:27:18.804 --> 00:27:21.222
So, perhaps you might try this.

377
00:27:22.558 --> 00:27:25.674
Oh, my uncle's producing
the film version.

378
00:27:25.687 --> 00:27:28.813
Alice in Wonderland
was originally a book.

379
00:27:29.315 --> 00:27:32.734
You might surprise yourself
and actually enjoy it.

380
00:27:32.818 --> 00:27:34.527
(SCOFFS) This is my punishment?

381
00:27:35.821 --> 00:27:37.280
This school is so weird.

382
00:27:37.406 --> 00:27:40.074
What do you want
to get out of this school, Poppy?

383
00:27:40.159 --> 00:27:42.702
To get out of this school.

384
00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:46.789
You know, this school has produced
absolutely nobody of note.

385
00:27:46.915 --> 00:27:51.044
Our leading light was the girl
who was Princess Diana's foot doctor.

386
00:27:51.128 --> 00:27:54.464
So, if your aim is to make
the pages of Us Weekly,

387
00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:57.091
then this isn't the place for you.

388
00:27:57.176 --> 00:28:01.888
What we do produce are smart,
independent, free-thinking,

389
00:28:01.972 --> 00:28:05.266
good-hearted girls
who remain friends for life.

390
00:28:07.353 --> 00:28:10.480
The kind of girl that, behind all
your wisecracks, I know you are.

391
00:28:12.441 --> 00:28:17.278
Run along now, I must get on.
My in-tray is piling up.

392
00:28:31.502 --> 00:28:34.128
Not brown enough. More coffee.

393
00:28:37.508 --> 00:28:38.591
(GRUNTS)

394
00:28:38.675 --> 00:28:40.468
More elbow grease.

395
00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:43.679
You're aging these clothes,
not stirring your tea.

396
00:28:43.806 --> 00:28:46.474
I need complete authenticity.

397
00:28:48.310 --> 00:28:49.560
(SIGHS)

398
00:28:50.396 --> 00:28:54.732
Charlotte heard Freddie say
I looked exactly like Keira Knightley.

399
00:29:05.869 --> 00:29:10.665
Right! That's done. Empty the water.

400
00:29:11.583 --> 00:29:14.544
Not that way, fool. You'll spill it.
Out the window.

401
00:29:14.670 --> 00:29:17.505
- Out the window?
- Just get on with it.

402
00:29:20.008 --> 00:29:21.259
Are you sure?

403
00:29:21.343 --> 00:29:23.136
(POPPY GASPS)

404
00:29:25.848 --> 00:29:26.889
(GASPS)

405
00:29:27.182 --> 00:29:31.436
So sorry.
Just can't trust the help these days.

406
00:29:32.104 --> 00:29:34.397
Do you have a pass
to be out during lessons?

407
00:29:34.523 --> 00:29:40.945
- Oh, yeah, I do. It's right here!
- Well, don't walk on the grass.

408
00:29:51.540 --> 00:29:52.748
(SIGHS)

409
00:30:17.274 --> 00:30:20.568
For the tenth time,
you need to make your bed.

410
00:30:22.154 --> 00:30:28.659
Jesus. What's so bloody hard?
Pick up. Put down. It's not rocket science.

411
00:30:44.259 --> 00:30:46.302
Sit down. I'll do that.

412
00:30:49.848 --> 00:30:51.182
Thanks.

413
00:30:53.685 --> 00:30:56.155
You're freezing.
You need a jumper.

414
00:30:56.168 --> 00:30:58.648
Whatever that is, I
don't think I have one.

415
00:30:59.107 --> 00:31:02.777
I don't think I have anything
thicker than prosciutto.

416
00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:12.954
Thanks. I didn't really come prepared.
Didn't figure I'd be here this long.

417
00:31:14.289 --> 00:31:18.167
Nothing worse than the only message you
get all day being from the phone company.

418
00:31:18.293 --> 00:31:20.378
But Matron took all the phones.

419
00:31:21.046 --> 00:31:24.674
No. She took all your phones.
She took our decoys.

420
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:28.886
She has no idea that none of them work.
We keep our real phones hidden.

421
00:31:30.305 --> 00:31:34.809
Here. Call your parents. Call your
therapist. Knock yourself out.

422
00:31:35.978 --> 00:31:39.647
But why would you do this for me?
You think I'm a total asshole.

423
00:31:39.731 --> 00:31:43.651
No, you behave like an arsehole.
There's a difference.

424
00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:52.201
Look, I know that I'm not
some Malibu therapist,

425
00:31:52.327 --> 00:31:57.582
but I can guess that you're feeling scared
and a little bit homesick.

426
00:31:59.001 --> 00:32:04.338
Which, in my experience, doesn't actually
make you a bad person. Just a normal one.

427
00:32:10.178 --> 00:32:11.846
Sweet photo.

428
00:32:13.682 --> 00:32:15.349
Is it your mum?

429
00:32:18.020 --> 00:32:20.438
She going to come out and visit?

430
00:32:23.025 --> 00:32:26.068
She died in a car accident when I was 11.

431
00:32:28.280 --> 00:32:29.322
Oh.

432
00:32:36.747 --> 00:32:39.123
Poppy, I'm so sorry.

433
00:32:39.207 --> 00:32:42.543
I know you're not some
Malibu therapist, but...

434
00:32:57.601 --> 00:32:59.644
Listen.

435
00:32:59.728 --> 00:33:03.022
- Are you serious about
getting out of here? - Yeah.

436
00:33:03.106 --> 00:33:06.817
Then, you're going to have to get
yourself expelled.

437
00:33:06.902 --> 00:33:08.444
Okay.

438
00:33:08.528 --> 00:33:12.365
"Anybody disporting themselves
in an improper manner will be proposed

439
00:33:12.449 --> 00:33:17.203
- "for expulsion before the Honor Court."
- Wait. Honor Court?

440
00:33:17.287 --> 00:33:19.622
It's like a trial in front
of the whole school

441
00:33:19.706 --> 00:33:23.501
by your peers, your teachers,
the Head Girl, and Mrs. Kingsley.

442
00:33:23.585 --> 00:33:26.545
But I'm telling you, it
hardly ever happens.

443
00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:30.132
If you really want to get expelled,
you can't just rock the boat.

444
00:33:30.217 --> 00:33:31.842
You have to drive it up onto the rocks,

445
00:33:31.927 --> 00:33:34.637
set fire to the galley
and dance on the burning deck.

446
00:33:34.721 --> 00:33:38.349
- You have to take it all the way.
- Aye, aye, Captain.

447
00:33:39.434 --> 00:33:40.768
Make your calls.

448
00:33:45.190 --> 00:33:48.609
Tip for best reception.
On top of the cupboard.

449
00:33:51.405 --> 00:33:55.574
Hi, Ruby. I miss you.
I'm going to escape, though. I promise you.

450
00:33:55.659 --> 00:33:57.743
You have no idea what it's like here.

451
00:33:57.828 --> 00:34:00.830
Ew! Who is she?

452
00:34:00.914 --> 00:34:06.085
Zero lip gloss upkeep,
and what's with the sweater from Target?

453
00:34:06.461 --> 00:34:08.295
I wish you could come and rescue me.

454
00:34:08.380 --> 00:34:11.298
She is such a romantic, Roddy.

455
00:34:11.383 --> 00:34:13.592
Take care of Roddy for me.

456
00:34:13.885 --> 00:34:15.553
(PHONE BEEPS)

457
00:34:15.637 --> 00:34:17.972
You already have. Let's hit the pool.

458
00:34:21.727 --> 00:34:23.310
(CREAKING)

459
00:34:24.604 --> 00:34:25.938
(OWL HOOTING)

460
00:34:26.022 --> 00:34:27.273
(GASPS)

461
00:34:34.740 --> 00:34:36.240
(POPPY SHRIEKS)

462
00:34:37.284 --> 00:34:40.453
Watch it, Wee Willie Winkie,
you'll set us all alight.

463
00:34:40.537 --> 00:34:42.413
Now, I've had a word with the girls.

464
00:34:42.497 --> 00:34:46.208
True, some of them took
a little more convincing than others.

465
00:34:46.293 --> 00:34:49.170
But it's decided. We're going to help you.

466
00:34:49.254 --> 00:34:52.423
We're your very own crack unit.
Operation Freedom.

467
00:34:52.507 --> 00:34:54.800
- Kiki, please explain.
- Right.

468
00:34:54.885 --> 00:34:58.971
We'll commence with an entry-level basic
favorite. Just to get warmed up.

469
00:34:59.055 --> 00:35:01.348
POPPY: It smells like pee in here.
KIKI: Does not smell like pee.

470
00:35:01.433 --> 00:35:02.600
(GREETING IN FRENCH)

471
00:35:02.684 --> 00:35:03.893
(GIRLS GREETING IN FRENCH)

472
00:35:03.977 --> 00:35:06.729
KIKI: But it's no good
just playing the same old tricks.

473
00:35:06.813 --> 00:35:10.483
Try to be as imaginative as possible.

474
00:35:10.567 --> 00:35:16.197
Only do things that will get you noticed.
Vary your targets as much as you can.

475
00:35:16.281 --> 00:35:20.367
And although we'll all be helping you,
the important thing to remember...

476
00:35:20.452 --> 00:35:21.494
GIRL: Harriet!

477
00:35:21.578 --> 00:35:25.498
KIKI: is that you have to get the blame
for everything.

478
00:35:25.582 --> 00:35:26.957
Run along.

479
00:35:28.001 --> 00:35:29.293
Speaking.

480
00:35:29.377 --> 00:35:31.337
MR. NELLIST: Headphones on, girls.

481
00:35:33.048 --> 00:35:36.926
Come on, everybody. Don't run too fast
in your flip-flops. We'll just jump in,

482
00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:40.346
have a quick paddle about, warm up,
then have tea and crumpets, yes?

483
00:35:40.430 --> 00:35:43.682
Yes, I'm in school right now.

484
00:35:43.767 --> 00:35:46.977
Regulation uniform.
Skirt just below the knee.

485
00:35:47.354 --> 00:35:48.646
(SCOFFS)

486
00:35:49.022 --> 00:35:50.940
Of course.

487
00:35:51.024 --> 00:35:55.611
They are a simple polyester.
Sturdy and practical.

488
00:35:55.695 --> 00:36:00.533
No, I have certainly not been naughty.
My disciplinary record is exemplary.

489
00:36:02.327 --> 00:36:03.869
Are you okay?

490
00:36:05.956 --> 00:36:08.207
SARA: Get out. Get out!

491
00:36:09.709 --> 00:36:12.253
Please, get out.

492
00:36:12.337 --> 00:36:14.171
(SARA WHISTLING)

493
00:36:18.134 --> 00:36:20.261
(GIRLS READING IN FRENCH)

494
00:36:32.107 --> 00:36:34.692
(STUTTERING) Yes, thank you very much.
That's it. Thank you.

495
00:36:34.776 --> 00:36:37.403
KIKI: If you make enough
of a nuisance of yourself...

496
00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:40.531
Poppy Moore!

497
00:36:40.615 --> 00:36:44.869
KIKI: she will eventually bow to pressure,
and she'll have to call your father.

498
00:36:44.953 --> 00:36:47.538
Naturally I'll call her father,
but she's had a difficult time.

499
00:36:47.622 --> 00:36:49.456
No, Sara, please. It's all right, dear.

500
00:36:49.541 --> 00:36:51.000
- Mr. Nellist.
- Sorry.

501
00:36:51.084 --> 00:36:56.964
KIKI: And then, with any luck,
she'll recommend you to the Honor Court.

502
00:36:57.257 --> 00:37:00.342
Unbe-bloody-lievable!

503
00:37:01.136 --> 00:37:04.763
She's got more lives than a Buddhist cat.

504
00:37:04.848 --> 00:37:07.808
Kingsley's not even
mentioned Honor Court.

505
00:37:07.893 --> 00:37:11.562
- I think people are starting to like her.
- HARRIET: People?

506
00:37:11.646 --> 00:37:15.065
People can learn to get used
to rotting pig's vomit

507
00:37:15.150 --> 00:37:18.861
- if they live with it for long enough.
- Maybe she's trying to leave.

508
00:37:18.945 --> 00:37:22.781
It'd be a nightmare if she stayed.
She makes a mockery of the system.

509
00:37:22.866 --> 00:37:26.035
She's not staying. Take it from me.

510
00:37:26.119 --> 00:37:30.247
Five generations of my family
have made this school great.

511
00:37:30.332 --> 00:37:34.168
The school motto is
scholarship, fellowship, loyalty.

512
00:37:34.252 --> 00:37:39.757
Not be a slutty, whore-y shit-brain.

513
00:37:39.841 --> 00:37:42.343
So brilliante, Harriet.

514
00:37:42.427 --> 00:37:44.929
SARA: Mr. Nellist, don't cry.
Maybe a tissue.

515
00:37:45.013 --> 00:37:46.931
MR. NELLIST: (CRYING)
I can't stand her. It's driving me crazy.

516
00:37:47.015 --> 00:37:50.726
Perhaps a strong cup of tea. I'm only sorry
it can't be something stronger.

517
00:37:50.810 --> 00:37:52.311
SARA: Cup of tea.

518
00:37:56.316 --> 00:37:57.900
POPPY: Come on, quick.

519
00:37:57.984 --> 00:37:59.568
(BOTH GIGGLING)

520
00:38:04.240 --> 00:38:07.701
- Quick. Give me the tape. Give
me the tape. - KATE: Quick.

521
00:38:08.453 --> 00:38:10.746
Pull the button off.

522
00:38:10.830 --> 00:38:13.916
- Oh, my God. There's a car.
- Quick.

523
00:38:29.140 --> 00:38:31.392
Whoa! It's all right, Cerberus. Only me.

524
00:38:31.476 --> 00:38:35.229
- Who's Cerberus?
- The dog that guards the gates of hell.

525
00:38:38.066 --> 00:38:42.569
- (WHISPERING) Go, go. Get away.
- Hurry up. Or you'll disturb my girls.

526
00:38:46.574 --> 00:38:48.200
(SNEEZING)

527
00:38:50.078 --> 00:38:52.246
(IMITATES SNEEZING)

528
00:38:52.956 --> 00:38:55.290
Sorry, terrible allergies.

529
00:38:57.043 --> 00:38:58.752
(FLATULENT SOUND)

530
00:38:59.713 --> 00:39:03.966
Oh, sorry. Better an empty house
than an angry tenant, right?

531
00:39:08.263 --> 00:39:11.087
I don't get it. It's like
you've got immunity.

532
00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:13.934
Your dad's a Mafia
guy or something.

533
00:39:14.519 --> 00:39:16.979
Yup. I'm the Goddaughter.

534
00:39:17.063 --> 00:39:20.524
Whatever it is,
she's cutting you a lot of slack.

535
00:39:20.608 --> 00:39:26.947
We need to up the ante. In fact,
we need to focus on her big weakness.

536
00:39:27.949 --> 00:39:30.159
Oh, my God. You have to snog Freddie.

537
00:39:30.243 --> 00:39:33.120
Snog? That sounds disgusting.
What is that?

538
00:39:33.204 --> 00:39:36.915
- It's English for make out.
- Mrs. Kingsley will go ballistic.

539
00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:42.171
- And Harriet would have an absolute fit.
- Well, that's a definite bonus.

540
00:39:42.255 --> 00:39:44.673
- KATE: And he'll be at the social.
- Cool.

541
00:39:44.758 --> 00:39:47.801
Just remember, the point is to get caught.

542
00:39:47.886 --> 00:39:49.595
All right, so, what's the
deal with the social?

543
00:39:49.679 --> 00:39:51.680
It's the school dance on Saturday night.

544
00:39:51.765 --> 00:39:56.268
Traditionally, it's fancy dress.
This year, it's Movie Magic.

545
00:39:56.352 --> 00:40:02.191
But the only ones who bother to dress up
are teachers, morons, and Harriet.

546
00:40:02.275 --> 00:40:06.612
I say we dress up fancy. Real fancy.

547
00:40:06.696 --> 00:40:09.490
This mission needs to be planned precisely.

548
00:40:09.574 --> 00:40:12.201
- Kiki?
- Okay.

549
00:40:12.285 --> 00:40:18.165
Operation Freedom, part two, step one.
Attract Freddie.

550
00:40:18.291 --> 00:40:22.294
Step one, subsection A, look the part.

551
00:40:23.004 --> 00:40:26.590
Kiki, you're actually making something
quite exciting sound like physics homework.

552
00:40:26.674 --> 00:40:27.716
(GIRLS GIGGLING)

553
00:40:27.801 --> 00:40:31.220
Basically, we're going into town,
and we're going to get some killer outfits.

554
00:40:31.304 --> 00:40:34.014
DRIPPY: I want something
that says, "Elegant",

555
00:40:34.099 --> 00:40:38.352
"but at the same time
incredibly slutty and available."

556
00:40:38.436 --> 00:40:41.605
In fact, I'm not that
bothered about elegant.

557
00:40:57.038 --> 00:41:00.541
POPPY: So apparently, the key is to hook up
with the headmistress' son.

558
00:41:00.625 --> 00:41:04.128
I'll do your trick, Rubes.
Swing my hips and giggle.

559
00:41:04.212 --> 00:41:06.296
Oh, come on, Poppy.
We're going to miss the bus.

560
00:41:06.381 --> 00:41:09.216
Don't forget to log off now, you ninny.

561
00:41:12.971 --> 00:41:16.640
Everyone, sign out. Remember you are
representatives of the school.

562
00:41:16.724 --> 00:41:21.228
- Sign your own name. Come on.
- Poppy Moore. What are you wearing?

563
00:41:21.312 --> 00:41:24.648
You are going into town,
not appearing in a window in Amsterdam.

564
00:41:24.732 --> 00:41:26.984
- Change immediately.
- I don't have anything else.

565
00:41:27.068 --> 00:41:30.445
I thought you might be quite concerned
by that attire, Matron.

566
00:41:30.530 --> 00:41:33.949
So we had a little look-see
in lost property on our way here.

567
00:41:34.033 --> 00:41:36.368
- Didn't we?
- We did.

568
00:41:39.122 --> 00:41:40.873
It'll suit you.

569
00:41:42.458 --> 00:41:44.251
Promise.

570
00:41:46.629 --> 00:41:47.838
(GIRL BARKING)

571
00:41:47.922 --> 00:41:49.173
(GIRLS LAUGHING)

572
00:41:49.257 --> 00:41:51.800
DRIPPY: Well, that's cute.
My grandma used to have a dog just like it.

573
00:41:51.885 --> 00:41:55.220
KIKI: Poppy, I think your jumper
is the cat's pajamas.

574
00:42:04.230 --> 00:42:08.567
BUS CONDUCTOR: Come on, girls. In you go.
Hurry up. Upstairs.

575
00:42:14.616 --> 00:42:18.785
Don't push. Don't push. Plenty of room.
Come on. Here we go.

576
00:42:18.870 --> 00:42:21.788
- Come on, Poppy! Jump!
- GIRLS: Poppy! Jump!

577
00:42:21.873 --> 00:42:25.667
I can't find my sanitizer!
I can't find my sanitizer!

578
00:42:25.752 --> 00:42:28.754
- You left it in the dorm!
- Oh, my God, no!

579
00:42:35.011 --> 00:42:36.053
Ew!

580
00:42:36.137 --> 00:42:37.221
GIRLS: Ew!

581
00:42:40.975 --> 00:42:43.101
(GIRLS CHATTERING)

582
00:42:43.186 --> 00:42:44.728
Oh, my God, look.

583
00:42:44.812 --> 00:42:47.814
(HEAVY METAL MUSIC
BLARING ON CAR STEREO)

584
00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:07.292
(DOGS BARKING)

585
00:43:10.338 --> 00:43:12.172
- GIRLS: Oh, hello.
- Hi.

586
00:43:12.298 --> 00:43:14.508
Ew! Gross!

587
00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:19.638
- Where are we going?
- To our favorite shop.

588
00:43:19.722 --> 00:43:21.056
Cancer research?

589
00:43:21.182 --> 00:43:24.351
Girls, I'm all about finding a cure,
but considering I flunked chemistry,

590
00:43:24.477 --> 00:43:28.730
I don't know how much help I'm going to be.
And BTW, which, FYI, means "By the way",

591
00:43:28.856 --> 00:43:32.943
- this is supposed to be shopping time.
- We're not going to be doing the research.

592
00:43:33.027 --> 00:43:36.863
This is a charity shop.
The money goes to charity.

593
00:43:36.990 --> 00:43:38.699
Oh, I just had a heart palpitation.

594
00:43:38.825 --> 00:43:42.452
You guys are so adorable, but we need
to look really hot for the social.

595
00:43:42.537 --> 00:43:46.331
- So let's go hit Oxford Street.
- I take it you flunked geography, too.

596
00:43:46.416 --> 00:43:50.377
Oxford Street is in London, my friend.
This is your lot.

597
00:43:52.672 --> 00:43:54.339
(GIRLS LAUGHING)

598
00:43:57.510 --> 00:44:00.554
KIKI: Josie, take that big bra off my head.
JOSIE: No!

599
00:44:02.056 --> 00:44:06.810
- Hey, Kate! What about this for Ascot?
- KATE: Magnificent.

600
00:44:06.894 --> 00:44:09.187
Is this too workaday?

601
00:44:10.440 --> 00:44:15.027
Come on now, girls.
This is a serious mission. Get a move on.

602
00:44:15.111 --> 00:44:19.031
Now, Poppy, how about something
like this? Fifty pence.

603
00:44:19.115 --> 00:44:22.826
It looks like someone died in it. I'd
rather stay the Yorkshire Terrier freak.

604
00:44:22.910 --> 00:44:27.122
You're a Buddhist, right?
Think of it as clothing reincarnation.

605
00:44:27.248 --> 00:44:30.459
Honey, even Buddha wouldn't be
caught dead in half this stuff.

606
00:44:30.585 --> 00:44:35.422
Still, I guess anything's possible.
Come on. Let's do this.

607
00:44:36.466 --> 00:44:38.759
(POP SONG PLAYING)

608
00:45:34.190 --> 00:45:35.649
(ALL WHOOP)

609
00:45:36.692 --> 00:45:41.696
Unbelievable. This season Marni.
It's sophisticated, it's elegant.

610
00:45:41.823 --> 00:45:43.782
- Hot to trot?
- Check.

611
00:45:45.159 --> 00:45:48.578
If we could just call this stuff vintage
and add three zeros to the price tag,

612
00:45:48.663 --> 00:45:50.205
I could totally get into it.

613
00:45:50.331 --> 00:45:54.126
Perfection. Operation Freddie
is well and truly underway.

614
00:45:54.210 --> 00:45:57.087
Malibu moment.
Remember what I taught you guys?

615
00:45:57.171 --> 00:45:59.172
- Who are we?
- ALL: Who are we?

616
00:45:59.340 --> 00:45:59.965
(CAMERA CLICKING)

617
00:45:59.966 --> 00:46:00.424
(CAMERA CLICKING)

618
00:46:00.508 --> 00:46:04.594
MR. CHRISTOPHER: I think he's down,
the Penny Black. Yes, dated pre-war.

619
00:46:04.679 --> 00:46:09.516
- KATE: Really stupid ones.
- Oh, my God. It's Tom Cruise.

620
00:46:09.642 --> 00:46:12.602
Would you like to say that any louder?
I need your help.

621
00:46:12.687 --> 00:46:15.105
And I need a back wax
and a night with Michael Buble,

622
00:46:15.189 --> 00:46:19.234
but we don't always get what we want.
Trudy, attend to the brows.

623
00:46:19.861 --> 00:46:26.199
Yorkie fan. It's a nice dog, Yorkie.
I used to have one once. Wee Phillippe.

624
00:46:26.325 --> 00:46:28.827
Got savaged to death by a badger.

625
00:46:31.038 --> 00:46:35.167
- Aren't you the soufflé that didn't arise.
- Tell me about it. Okay.

626
00:46:35.251 --> 00:46:38.837
I need these extensions taken out,
a seriously deep conditioning.

627
00:46:38.921 --> 00:46:41.001
I'm thinking side bangs
with some buttery highlights,

628
00:46:41.048 --> 00:46:43.300
and maybe a few honey tones.

629
00:46:43.384 --> 00:46:47.471
And I'd like a night on Fireman Island,
but I'm afraid I'm whistling Dixie, okay?

630
00:46:47.555 --> 00:46:49.598
So here's what's on offer for you.

631
00:46:49.682 --> 00:46:51.850
- A tight perm.
- No.

632
00:46:51.934 --> 00:46:54.811
How about this? A wee bob.
That's fun, isn't it?

633
00:46:54.896 --> 00:46:56.771
- No.
- Okay. What about this?

634
00:46:56.856 --> 00:46:58.273
Oh, a pineapple.

635
00:46:58.357 --> 00:47:01.902
- Oh, Hawaii.
- No.

636
00:47:01.986 --> 00:47:05.280
What about something
a little bit more natural?

637
00:47:06.324 --> 00:47:09.284
- Natural?
- MR. CHRISTOPHER: Aye. The real you.

638
00:47:12.205 --> 00:47:14.831
- Natural it is.
- Radical.

639
00:47:14.916 --> 00:47:17.751
Okay. Ladies, let's do this.

640
00:47:19.629 --> 00:47:23.215
Oh, right now, we're gonna need
that, that, that.

641
00:47:25.343 --> 00:47:28.261
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

642
00:47:28.346 --> 00:47:34.059
Oh, no, I... Don't look at...
That's nof mine. Nope.

643
00:47:34.143 --> 00:47:37.938
Hey, Mummy.
Two strong teas, please, bella, pronto!

644
00:47:38.022 --> 00:47:39.272
(BLOW DRYER WHIRRING)

645
00:47:39.357 --> 00:47:41.900
Don't you look at me like that.

646
00:47:44.320 --> 00:47:45.737
Nix that.

647
00:47:47.031 --> 00:47:49.616
You ready? Okay.

648
00:47:52.411 --> 00:47:54.829
- Et voilà.
- Wow. Thank you.

649
00:47:54.914 --> 00:47:56.456
You're welcome, darling.

650
00:47:56.541 --> 00:48:00.961
I'm cream-crackered.
I'll lay down and have a wee satsuma.

651
00:48:01.045 --> 00:48:04.047
- You look so...
- English.

652
00:48:04.131 --> 00:48:07.676
- I look like my mom.
- Is she beautiful, too?

653
00:48:07.760 --> 00:48:12.889
- She was. Very.
- Sorry. Foot-in-mouth disease.

654
00:48:13.849 --> 00:48:15.517
(GIRLS LAUGHING)

655
00:48:16.227 --> 00:48:20.564
- Okay. Time for the juice. Any bright
ideas? - Leave it to me. I've got a plan.

656
00:48:26.529 --> 00:48:31.283
So, Susan, do you like your new office?

657
00:48:31.367 --> 00:48:36.663
I don't know what's worse,
my job or that husband of mine.

658
00:48:38.124 --> 00:48:41.501
Keith from Accounts is driving me crazy.

659
00:48:41.586 --> 00:48:45.046
He wants that report
on his desk by Thursday.

660
00:48:45.131 --> 00:48:47.382
What's the report about?

661
00:48:50.720 --> 00:48:53.054
- Business.
- (WHISPERS) What?

662
00:48:53.139 --> 00:48:56.766
Do you want to buy a carpet tomorrow?

663
00:48:56.851 --> 00:49:01.062
Yes. After I've dropped
the kids off at the pool.

664
00:49:02.356 --> 00:49:05.483
In my saloon car.

665
00:49:05.568 --> 00:49:09.237
Two bottles of Grizinski
and one of Donmatsa, please.

666
00:49:11.032 --> 00:49:13.450
And two Creme Eggs, please.

667
00:49:14.410 --> 00:49:15.535
(SCOFFS)

668
00:49:18.205 --> 00:49:20.624
Why did you order the Creme Eggs,
you idiot?

669
00:49:20.708 --> 00:49:23.710
Why did you only get two, Drippy?
Now, we've got to quarter them.

670
00:49:23.794 --> 00:49:26.338
- He believed us till then.
- Oh, yeah, right.

671
00:49:26.422 --> 00:49:30.091
Maybe if you hadn't asked me what
Keith's report was about. Where's Poppy?

672
00:49:30.635 --> 00:49:33.803
- Are you okay?
- I'm furious. Stupid Drippy.

673
00:49:33.888 --> 00:49:36.598
I know. Never mind. Let's go.

674
00:49:37.975 --> 00:49:39.934
(POP MUSIC PLAYING)

675
00:49:45.650 --> 00:49:50.403
Would you boys like a drink?
Now, anybody here? Come on.

676
00:49:54.033 --> 00:49:55.408
Hello, hello.

677
00:49:55.493 --> 00:50:00.664
Name's Nellist. Roger Nellist.
License to deejay.

678
00:50:01.999 --> 00:50:05.460
Gosh, you look like James Bond.

679
00:50:05.544 --> 00:50:07.087
I reckon you might like a fruit punch.

680
00:50:07.171 --> 00:50:10.090
Oh, I'll have it shaken and not stirred.

681
00:50:14.334 --> 00:50:15.655
OLD LADY: Why aren't you dancing?

682
00:50:15.680 --> 00:50:18.181
They're all dressed up,
waiting for you over there.

683
00:50:19.850 --> 00:50:21.226
JANE: Mr. Nellist.

684
00:50:21.310 --> 00:50:22.602
- Harriet's coming.
- Harriet's coming.

685
00:50:22.687 --> 00:50:24.562
Right, yes, yes, yes.

686
00:50:29.151 --> 00:50:31.903
(SLOW INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

687
00:50:36.701 --> 00:50:38.535
(BOYS LAUGHING)

688
00:50:45.084 --> 00:50:47.585
Mr. Darcy.

689
00:50:47.670 --> 00:50:51.172
What undue pleasure it is
to be afforded your company.

690
00:50:51.257 --> 00:50:54.509
- Hi.
- You may only call me Mrs. Darcy

691
00:50:54.593 --> 00:50:58.763
when you are completely,
perfectly, incandescently happy.

692
00:50:59.557 --> 00:51:01.057
Okay. Cool.

693
