Something really bad has happened.

918
01:08:04.247 --> 01:08:10.085
Crap. Fashion emergency.
Got to go. See you soon as.

919
01:08:10.170 --> 01:08:12.713
- Love you.
- Love you more.

920
01:08:15.425 --> 01:08:18.927
Sorry, Roddy. Couldn't get rid of her.
What was I saying?

921
01:08:20.346 --> 01:08:25.809
- Roddy? Babe?
- No, Ruby. Still me. Babe.

922
01:08:29.189 --> 01:08:30.189
(SCOFFS)

923
01:08:33.526 --> 01:08:34.985
(SIGHING)

924
01:09:01.888 --> 01:09:03.180
Shit.

925
01:09:03.264 --> 01:09:05.349
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

926
01:09:05.433 --> 01:09:06.850
Shit.

927
01:09:20.740 --> 01:09:22.074
(PANTING)

928
01:09:36.756 --> 01:09:38.590
(SCREAMING)

929
01:09:50.144 --> 01:09:52.813
Kate. Kate, quick. Wake up.

930
01:09:52.939 --> 01:09:55.059
KATE: What's wrong now?
POPPY: I didn't mean to do it.

931
01:09:55.108 --> 01:09:57.693
It was an accident. I thought I put it out.
I thought I'd stopped it.

932
01:09:57.777 --> 01:09:59.820
I don't know what happened.
I didn't want to hurt anybody.

933
01:09:59.904 --> 01:10:01.810
Jesus, Poppy. You're
a proper psycho.

934
01:10:01.823 --> 01:10:03.740
Help me get everyone
up before it spreads.

935
01:10:03.825 --> 01:10:07.411
KATE: Josie. Josie, get up.
Josie, there's a fire. Get up.

936
01:10:08.121 --> 01:10:09.204
(FIRE ALARM RINGING)

937
01:10:09.289 --> 01:10:12.124
Fire! Fire, everyone get up!

938
01:10:12.250 --> 01:10:15.419
Fire! It's a real fire! Get out of bed!
Get up, it's a fire.

939
01:10:15.503 --> 01:10:17.796
This isn't a practice. You guys, get up.

940
01:10:17.922 --> 01:10:20.674
Come on, darling, get up.
It's a fire, it's not a drill.

941
01:10:21.467 --> 01:10:23.594
(SIRENS WAILING)

942
01:10:26.856 --> 01:10:28.616
KATE: Josie...
JOSIE: No, I'm not getting up!

943
01:10:28.641 --> 01:10:30.142
KATE: Get up, we're on fire!

944
01:10:30.268 --> 01:10:32.811
It's a real fire! Please, everybody get up!

945
01:10:39.360 --> 01:10:41.278
- Phoebe Faircloff.
- Here.

946
01:10:41.362 --> 01:10:43.322
- MRS. KINGSLEY: Susan Casey.
- Here.

947
01:10:43.489 --> 01:10:45.073
DRIPPY: Let me out! Let me out!

948
01:10:45.158 --> 01:10:46.533
(DRIPPY BANGING ON DOOR)

949
01:10:51.164 --> 01:10:52.956
FIREMAN 1: Check the pressure
on tank three.

950
01:10:53.041 --> 01:10:54.801
FIREMAN 2: Charlie, take
the first position.

951
01:10:54.876 --> 01:10:57.544
- Daisy Bevin?
- DAISY: Here.

952
01:10:57.629 --> 01:10:59.880
- Can't hear you, Daisy.
- Here.

953
01:11:05.720 --> 01:11:07.346
Jennifer Logan.

954
01:11:09.307 --> 01:11:12.351
Jennifer? Has anyone seen Drippy?

955
01:11:13.353 --> 01:11:15.979
Come on, girls!
Who was the last person to see Drippy?

956
01:11:16.064 --> 01:11:18.690
Freezer. Drippy's in the freezer!

957
01:11:19.067 --> 01:11:20.567
MRS. KINGSLEY: Poppy, come back.

958
01:11:21.819 --> 01:11:23.899
MRS. KINGSLEY: Stay back, girls.
FIREMAN 1: Stop her!

959
01:11:32.830 --> 01:11:34.873
POPPY: Drippy! Drippy!

960
01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:38.251
Drippy!

961
01:11:43.925 --> 01:11:45.717
GIRL 1: What's going on?

962
01:11:46.094 --> 01:11:47.886
(GIRLS CHATTERING)

963
01:11:55.561 --> 01:11:57.270
(POPPY COUGHING)

964
01:12:11.393 --> 01:12:13.513
MRS. KINGSLEY: You're a very foolish,
very brave girl.

965
01:12:13.538 --> 01:12:15.580
All right, off to the ambulance now.

966
01:12:16.416 --> 01:12:17.624
FREDDIE: My God.

967
01:12:18.960 --> 01:12:21.169
- What do you think happened?
- Don't know yet.

968
01:12:21.254 --> 01:12:24.256
We're lucky, could've been a lot worse.

969
01:12:33.266 --> 01:12:36.643
GIRL 1: Well done, Poppy.
GIRL 2: You saved us. You were brilliant.

970
01:12:43.609 --> 01:12:48.155
- Hey. I believe this is yours.
- GIRL 3: Thank you.

971
01:12:49.369 --> 01:12:51.009
Do you realize you could have killed her?

972
01:12:51.034 --> 01:12:52.492
GIRL 4: Thank you. Well done.
Thanks, Poppy.

973
01:12:52.577 --> 01:12:55.328
- You could have killed all of us.
- Didn't mean to.

974
01:12:55.455 --> 01:12:58.498
I thought I'd stopped it. I swear.

975
01:12:58.624 --> 01:13:02.169
I don't understand.
I heard footsteps, and then I put it out.

976
01:13:02.295 --> 01:13:06.465
I was just so upset at everything,
and I wish I hadn't done it.

977
01:13:08.468 --> 01:13:11.178
I really wish you hadn't done it, too.

978
01:13:15.141 --> 01:13:16.224
(SIGHING)

979
01:13:16.309 --> 01:13:19.644
MRS. KINGSLEY: Someone here knows
exactly what happened last night.

980
01:13:21.773 --> 01:13:25.317
What we're clear on is
that this fire was no accident.

981
01:13:26.277 --> 01:13:30.363
If you have the sense to own up,
no legal charges will be filed.

982
01:13:31.032 --> 01:13:34.659
If not, it will be passed on
to the local authorities.

983
01:13:36.162 --> 01:13:39.664
You have until the end of the day
to come forward.

984
01:14:10.196 --> 01:14:14.866
POPPY: Dear Freddie,
how can I begin to say I'm sorry?

985
01:14:14.992 --> 01:14:20.455
You are good and honest and true,
and, well, I'm the opposite.

986
01:14:20.540 --> 01:14:24.626
But I'm learning.
So now I'm going to do the right thing.

987
01:14:24.710 --> 01:14:26.503
And if it means I have to leave here,

988
01:14:26.587 --> 01:14:31.049
I just want you to know,
I promise you I never wrote that e-mail.

989
01:14:32.051 --> 01:14:35.220
For a moment there, yeah,
you were my ticket out of here.

990
01:14:35.346 --> 01:14:37.639
But then I got to know you.

991
01:14:37.723 --> 01:14:41.309
I have never felt this way before
about anyone

992
01:14:41.394 --> 01:14:43.979
and I really need you to know that.

993
01:14:45.731 --> 01:14:47.315
(EXHALES)

994
01:14:52.405 --> 01:14:53.738
MRS. KINGSLEY: Come in.

995
01:14:55.408 --> 01:14:57.409
Oh, what can I do for you, Poppy?

996
01:15:02.665 --> 01:15:08.753
It's what I used to start it. It was an
accident, and I thought I put it out.

997
01:15:08.838 --> 01:15:13.258
But I guess not. Obviously not.

998
01:15:13.342 --> 01:15:14.926
Oh, Poppy.

999
01:15:17.513 --> 01:15:20.265
You realize what this means, don't you?

1000
01:15:21.934 --> 01:15:25.562
- Will I be expelled?
- The Honor Court will decide,

1001
01:15:26.022 --> 01:15:30.859
but I suspect you'll understand
that it's just a formality at this point.

1002
01:15:30.943 --> 01:15:36.281
The weird thing is
I really did try to turn it around.

1003
01:15:36.407 --> 01:15:41.536
I didn't want to disappoint you.
I'm so sorry.

1004
01:15:44.707 --> 01:15:46.458
I'm so sorry, too.

1005
01:15:49.462 --> 01:15:53.256
Do you think maybe
you could give this to Freddie for me?

1006
01:16:08.731 --> 01:16:10.398
I told her it was me.

1007
01:16:10.483 --> 01:16:13.235
I'm going to the Honor Court,
and then I'll be leaving.

1008
01:16:13.319 --> 01:16:15.737
So, this is for you.

1009
01:16:15.821 --> 01:16:21.493
Well done. You finally got what you wanted.
You must be overjoyed.

1010
01:16:21.619 --> 01:16:26.414
- I couldn't be more unhappy.
- Please. Give it a rest.

1011
01:17:05.871 --> 01:17:07.122
POPPY: Mom?

1012
01:17:33.024 --> 01:17:36.901
- Hey, I've been looking for you.
- Hi.

1013
01:17:38.029 --> 01:17:42.657
- So you backed out of our deal.
- What deal?

1014
01:17:42.742 --> 01:17:46.661
- That you won't fry my head.
- Yeah.

1015
01:17:46.746 --> 01:17:49.289
(SNIFFLING) But you poached my heart.

1016
01:17:49.373 --> 01:17:52.375
Hey. Come on.

1017
01:17:55.254 --> 01:17:59.007
What if it doesn't have a moral?
Or says Alice.

1018
01:17:59.091 --> 01:18:03.178
I think I just fell down the rabbit hole
and found it.

1019
01:18:03.262 --> 01:18:04.512
Look.

1020
01:18:08.434 --> 01:18:13.605
- She looks exactly like you.
- Yeah. She was my mom.

1021
01:18:13.731 --> 01:18:17.609
She went to this school.
I didn't even know.

1022
01:18:24.950 --> 01:18:28.286
Well, guess it's time
to face the music now.

1023
01:18:37.755 --> 01:18:38.755
(GIRLS ARGUING)

1024
01:18:38.756 --> 01:18:40.715
(GIRLS ARGUING)

1025
01:18:41.133 --> 01:18:44.010
Josie, I'm never wrong.
When am I ever wrong?

1026
01:18:44.095 --> 01:18:45.387
You're wrong when we did
the math challenge.

1027
01:18:45.471 --> 01:18:50.100
Hey! She's confessed.
She's going to Honor Court this afternoon.

1028
01:18:50.184 --> 01:18:52.727
- That's brave.
- And really stupid.

1029
01:18:52.812 --> 01:18:54.854
Because guess what I've discovered.

1030
01:18:55.981 --> 01:19:00.860
It is with great regret and sadness
that we call the Honor Court to session.

1031
01:19:02.947 --> 01:19:07.951
The e-mails were sent 11:40 in the morning.
But according to Drippy,

1032
01:19:08.035 --> 01:19:11.454
Poppy left the computer room
a few minutes after 11:00.

1033
01:19:11.539 --> 01:19:14.874
I got my 11:00 Wagon Wheel, then I
went to tell her Freddie was waiting.

1034
01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:16.543
She left immediately.

1035
01:19:16.669 --> 01:19:19.754
I was able to access the keystroke order
of the root file

1036
01:19:19.839 --> 01:19:22.590
to find out
who else was logged on there then.

1037
01:19:22.675 --> 01:19:27.512
- And guess who the only other person was?
- Who?

1038
01:19:27.888 --> 01:19:30.765
It will henceforth be
our job to objectively

1039
01:19:30.850 --> 01:19:34.853
and dispassionately ascertain
what happened that fateful night

1040
01:19:34.979 --> 01:19:40.316
that will hence to forth long blight
the memory of this proud institution.

1041
01:19:40.651 --> 01:19:43.653
And when you think about it,
Poppy would never say "term."

1042
01:19:43.737 --> 01:19:45.572
She calls it a bloody samosa or something.

1043
01:19:45.698 --> 01:19:49.367
- "Semester."
- Whatever. Anyway, to check the reality,

1044
01:19:49.994 --> 01:19:53.538
I had a sneaky look
in her diary for Friday's entry.

1045
01:19:53.664 --> 01:19:56.332
KATE: Don't do that.
DRIPPY: Shut up and listen.

1046
01:19:57.710 --> 01:20:04.257
"I think, deep breath, I kind of love them
like proper friends I've known forever.

1047
01:20:04.341 --> 01:20:07.427
"They've made me say words
like "horridious" and "herbal".

1048
01:20:07.511 --> 01:20:10.972
"Which is sort of whack, and I'd probably
hate them if I wasn't one of them."

1049
01:20:11.056 --> 01:20:13.892
"But I like that I am now one of them."

1050
01:20:16.103 --> 01:20:19.314
Apart from some
atrocious spelling mistakes,

1051
01:20:19.398 --> 01:20:23.318
it's all a bit more
kosher, don't you think?

1052
01:20:23.402 --> 01:20:26.571
And now she's going to get thrown out.

1053
01:20:27.406 --> 01:20:29.491
It is your duty

1054
01:20:29.575 --> 01:20:33.661
to understand the dark forces
that drove a seemingly...

1055
01:20:33.746 --> 01:20:37.165
Harriet? May I remind you
that the honor court

1056
01:20:37.249 --> 01:20:39.501
is no place
for your personal grandstanding,

1057
01:20:39.585 --> 01:20:41.753
and that Poppy has a right to speak
in her own defense

1058
01:20:41.879 --> 01:20:44.506
before the court as a whole
passes judgment?

1059
01:20:44.590 --> 01:20:46.716
Thank you, Mrs. Kingsley.

1060
01:20:48.385 --> 01:20:52.764
I won't insult everybody
by trying to defend myself or my actions.

1061
01:20:59.271 --> 01:21:04.859
So, I think it's safe to say that
I've really messed up.

1062
01:21:04.944 --> 01:21:10.782
And I apologize profusely.
But I'm also so grateful to you all.

1063
01:21:12.409 --> 01:21:15.036
I tried really hard to
get out of this school,

1064
01:21:15.120 --> 01:21:19.207
and only now do I realize
just how much I want to stay.

1065
01:21:21.293 --> 01:21:25.880
I've learned so much being here.
Being with all of you.

1066
01:21:25.965 --> 01:21:30.134
And in some ways being with my mom,

1067
01:21:30.261 --> 01:21:34.889
who I found out was
actually a student here.

1068
01:21:34.974 --> 01:21:37.392
I've had a hole in my heart for five years,

1069
01:21:37.476 --> 01:21:43.398
and somehow being here,
it slowly started to heal.

1070
01:21:43.482 --> 01:21:47.735
I know I may have looked
like a California girl,

1071
01:21:47.820 --> 01:21:52.282
but in my heart I've discovered
that I really am an Abbey Mount girl.

1072
01:21:56.328 --> 01:21:58.746
Objection! Sustained.

1073
01:21:58.831 --> 01:22:01.916
The court will heretofore disregard
the previous statement

1074
01:22:02.001 --> 01:22:05.670
and perhaps heretofore
we can begin the real business.

1075
01:22:05.754 --> 01:22:08.423
Can you tell us, in your own words,

1076
01:22:08.507 --> 01:22:10.925
where were you
on the aforementioned evening of...

1077
01:22:11.010 --> 01:22:14.178
Honestly, Harriet.
Who else's words do you expect her to use?

1078
01:22:14.263 --> 01:22:18.725
- Just leave this to me.
- Right. Sustained.

1079
01:22:20.019 --> 01:22:23.855
Poppy, were you in the cook's sitting room
on the night of the fire?

1080
01:22:23.981 --> 01:22:26.190
Yes, I was.

1081
01:22:26.275 --> 01:22:29.611
- Were you there with permission?
- No. I was not.

1082
01:22:29.695 --> 01:22:36.242
- Quiet, please. Silence in court.
- Did you intend on starting a fire?

1083
01:22:36.952 --> 01:22:39.203
- Not really.
- Objection!

1084
01:22:39.330 --> 01:22:43.249
- Does the defendant mean yes or no?
- Harriet.

1085
01:22:43.334 --> 01:22:46.628
It means no,
I had no intention of actually doing it.

1086
01:22:46.712 --> 01:22:50.715
- Was anyone else with you?
- Not as far as I know.

1087
01:22:50.841 --> 01:22:52.383
I was.

1088
01:22:53.469 --> 01:22:54.802
I was.

1089
01:22:54.887 --> 01:22:57.221
- I was.
- I was.

1090
01:22:57.348 --> 01:22:59.641
- GIRL 1: I was.
- I was.

1091
01:22:59.725 --> 01:23:01.142
- I was.
- GIRL 2: I was.

1092
01:23:01.226 --> 01:23:02.310
GIRLS: I was.

1093
01:23:02.394 --> 01:23:03.686
GIRLS: I was.

1094
01:23:03.771 --> 01:23:04.896
GIRLS: I was.

1095
01:23:04.980 --> 01:23:08.232
Objection! Stop! Order!

1096
01:23:08.317 --> 01:23:09.817
- I was.
- HARRIET: Stop it!

1097
01:23:09.902 --> 01:23:11.527
- GIRL 3: (WHISPERS) Come on.
- I was.

1098
01:23:12.738 --> 01:23:17.784
This is ridiculous!
What are you all doing? You're lying.

1099
01:23:17.868 --> 01:23:21.788
- They're lying, Mrs. Kingsley.
- Harriet, you're going down, biatch.

1100
01:23:21.872 --> 01:23:26.000
This is a conspiracy.
You can't expel the whole year,

1101
01:23:26.085 --> 01:23:31.839
- and they know that.
- Be quiet, Harriet! Sit down, everyone.

1102
01:23:31.924 --> 01:23:36.844
It's a black-and-white case.
She has to be expelled.

1103
01:23:36.929 --> 01:23:41.933
The girl set fire to the school,
endangering all our precious lives.

1104
01:23:42.059 --> 01:23:46.938
She walked in there, lighter at the ready,
and tried to burn the place down.

1105
01:23:47.022 --> 01:23:49.357
- Lighter?
- Not now, Jane.

1106
01:23:49.441 --> 01:23:53.361
- Have respect for court protocol.
- What lighter, Harriet?

1107
01:23:53.445 --> 01:23:56.531
Jesus, Charlotte,
how daft can you possibly be?

1108
01:23:56.615 --> 01:24:02.453
That ridiculous "I heart LA" lighter of
hers. She left it behind, for God's sakes.

1109
01:24:02.579 --> 01:24:09.210
Except, how do you know that, Harriet?
No one's mentioned a lighter before.

1110
01:24:09.294 --> 01:24:12.130
What? Yes, they have.

1111
01:24:12.965 --> 01:24:18.386
- Objection.
- Actually, Harriet, they haven't.

1112
01:24:18.470 --> 01:24:24.434
I have to second Jane's question, Harriet.
How did you know about that lighter?

1113
01:24:25.310 --> 01:24:27.478
Well, I...

1114
01:24:27.563 --> 01:24:30.565
Freddie found the lighter
before anyone saw it.

1115
01:24:30.649 --> 01:24:35.445
How could you possibly know unless...
Unless you were there?

1116
01:24:37.614 --> 01:24:40.908
This is absurd. I refuse to sit
here and listen to these wild...

1117
01:24:40.993 --> 01:24:46.164
I had put it out. And I heard footsteps.
It must have been you.

1118
01:24:46.290 --> 01:24:49.250
Oh, my God.
You restarted the fire, didn't you?

1119
01:24:49.334 --> 01:24:52.170
- Harriet, is this true?
- Of course not.

1120
01:24:52.254 --> 01:24:57.383
It all makes sense now. I knew it.
I think I'm innocent.

1121
01:24:57.468 --> 01:24:59.761
- We think so, too.
- You're not!

1122
01:24:59.845 --> 01:25:01.345
You awful bitch!

1123
01:25:01.430 --> 01:25:04.682
You've turned this school upside down.
You've ruined everything.

1124
01:25:04.808 --> 01:25:08.186
You started it.
I only finished what you started!

1125
01:25:08.312 --> 01:25:12.648
Harriet? My office, now.

1126
01:25:13.108 --> 01:25:14.859
(HARRIET GASPING)

1127
01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:31.709
(GIRLS CHEERING)

1128
01:25:34.004 --> 01:25:37.548
Okay, suckers, show time.
Let's open a can of whoop-ass.

1129
01:25:37.633 --> 01:25:38.883
(GIRLS CHANTING)

1130
01:25:38.967 --> 01:25:40.510
POPPY: You can do it.

1131
01:25:44.223 --> 01:25:46.307
GIRL 1: Let's go, Abbey Mount!

1132
01:25:48.727 --> 01:25:50.394
Come on, girls.

1133
01:25:52.689 --> 01:25:54.398
GIRL 2: Take it. Come on!

1134
01:25:57.736 --> 01:25:59.153
(WHISTLES)

1135
01:26:00.405 --> 01:26:03.574
Come on, guys.
We can bring it back. Let's go.

1136
01:26:09.581 --> 01:26:10.748
POPPY: You got it!

1137
01:26:11.750 --> 01:26:14.919
- Mrs. Kingsley?
- Oh, Mr. Moore, you made it.

1138
01:26:15.003 --> 01:26:16.754
- GERRY: Yes, I did.
- Please, come and take a seat.

1139
01:26:16.839 --> 01:26:18.923
- Did I miss much?
- Not at all.

1140
01:26:21.218 --> 01:26:24.428
- Where's Poppy?
- She's right there.

1141
01:26:48.745 --> 01:26:52.081
She's the spitting image of her mother,
isn't she?

1142
01:26:53.458 --> 01:26:55.751
She most certainly is.

1143
01:27:00.132 --> 01:27:03.384
Come on, Abbey Mount!
Take it out there. Come on.

1144
01:27:03.969 --> 01:27:05.428
(SHOUTING)

1145
01:27:17.649 --> 01:27:19.692
Come on, Abbey Mount. Let's go!

1146
01:27:19.776 --> 01:27:21.360
(REFEREE WHISTLING)

1147
01:27:21.445 --> 01:27:24.989
GIRLS: Two, four, six, eight
Stowe girls are really great

1148
01:27:27.659 --> 01:27:31.871
I don't know. You're trying really hard.
It's just great, great, great.

1149
01:27:31.955 --> 01:27:34.790
STOWE COACH: We're two-nil up.
They've got no possession whatsoever.

1150
01:27:34.875 --> 01:27:36.542
(GIRLS LAUGHING)

1151
01:27:38.170 --> 01:27:42.423
All right, ladies.
There's only one thing for it. Let's go.

1152
01:27:44.176 --> 01:27:45.343
Who are we?

1153
01:27:45.427 --> 01:27:46.827
- Abbey Mount!
- GIRLS: Abbey Mount!

1154
01:27:46.845 --> 01:27:47.929
POPPY: Who are we?

1155
01:27:48.013 --> 01:27:49.413
- Abbey Mount!
- GIRLS: Abbey Mount!

1156
01:27:49.431 --> 01:27:50.514
POPPY: What are we?

1157
01:27:50.641 --> 01:27:55.353
A leading single-sex school
admitting boarders at age 11.

1158
01:27:55.479 --> 01:27:57.772
Wrong! We're winners!

1159
01:27:58.315 --> 01:28:00.107
(FAST UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

1160
01:28:00.192 --> 01:28:02.276
(GIRLS SCREAMING)

1161
01:28:30.389 --> 01:28:33.307
- GIRL 1: Come on!
- Pass it, Poppy!

1162
01:28:40.899 --> 01:28:43.234
Come along, girls. Well done.

1163
01:28:51.660 --> 01:28:53.995
- Abbey Mount.
- GIRLS: Abbey Mount.

1164
01:28:56.999 --> 01:28:59.041
GIRL 2: Pass to Poppy, quick.

1165
01:29:03.338 --> 01:29:04.588
Come on, Poppy.

1166
01:29:05.590 --> 01:29:07.258
(GIRLS GRUNTING)

1167
01:29:21.398 --> 01:29:23.607
This is our last chance.
Let's make it count!

1168
01:29:34.036 --> 01:29:35.202
Kiki!

1169
01:29:36.121 --> 01:29:37.371
Drippy!

1170
01:29:37.456 --> 01:29:41.459
Why would you pass it to me? Oh, my God.
Okay. Somebody, help me.

1171
01:29:41.543 --> 01:29:46.172
Where is everyone? Who do I pass it to?
Jane! Jane! Where are you?

1172
01:29:46.256 --> 01:29:47.590
(GROANS)

1173
01:29:49.926 --> 01:29:51.802
(SCREAMING)

1174
01:29:53.638 --> 01:29:55.473
(REFEREE WHISTLING)

1175
01:30:03.815 --> 01:30:07.151
- Yes!
- They did it, they did it! Yes!

1176
01:30:07.235 --> 01:30:10.154
I told you, you could do it. I told you.

1177
01:30:19.164 --> 01:30:20.414
GERRY: Poppy.

1178
01:30:22.501 --> 01:30:28.589
Dad? My dad! My dad!
What are you doing here?

1179
01:30:28.673 --> 01:30:33.260
Mrs. Kingsley called.
She told me you found out about Mom.

1180
01:30:33.345 --> 01:30:34.929
Why didn't you just tell me, Dad?

1181
01:30:35.013 --> 01:30:38.933
I'm sorry, Poppy.
I thought it might make you too sad.

1182
01:30:39.017 --> 01:30:42.686
I did know that you needed to breathe
a different kind of air, though.

1183
01:30:43.855 --> 01:30:45.856
Did I do the right thing?

1184
01:30:45.982 --> 01:30:49.360
You did. Did you know Mom
was captain of the lacrosse team?

1185
01:30:49.444 --> 01:30:50.528
Yes.

1186
01:30:52.155 --> 01:30:57.785
And I also know that she is
incredibly proud of you right now.

1187
01:30:58.870 --> 01:31:00.162
As am I.

1188
01:31:07.879 --> 01:31:10.548
Daddy, put your back into it.

1189
01:31:10.674 --> 01:31:13.634
BOTH: Harriet. We think you forgot this.

1190
01:31:14.719 --> 01:31:16.554
Methinks so, too.

1191
01:31:18.223 --> 01:31:19.390
Mummy!

1192
01:31:20.058 --> 01:31:22.143
(POP MUSIC PLAYING)

1193
01:31:23.562 --> 01:31:25.146
GIRLS: Who are we?

1194
01:31:46.376 --> 01:31:47.751
Fire!

1195
01:32:30.754 --> 01:32:31.962
(SIGHS)

1196
01:32:32.297 --> 01:32:34.089
Major bloody SULA.

1197
01:32:38.220 --> 01:32:40.262
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

1198
01:32:43.975 --> 01:32:46.977
- Who's Ruby?
- (SCOFFS) Nobody.

1199
01:32:48.104 --> 01:32:50.606
Just some horridious cow I used to know.

1200
01:32:58.907 --> 01:33:01.825
- Can't do it.
- No way!

1201
01:33:01.952 --> 01:33:03.827
You're completely insane.

1202
01:33:03.954 --> 01:33:05.955
- Are you guys ready?
- KATE: No.

1203
01:33:06.498 --> 01:33:07.498
One.

1204
01:33:07.624 --> 01:33:08.999
- Two, three.
- GIRLS: Two, three.

1205
01:33:09.125 --> 01:33:10.834
(GIRLS SCREAMING)
